.TH KAGI-BUILD 1 "November 2026" "Kagi 0.39.0" "Developer Commands"
.SH NAME
kagi-build \- build Kagi in release mode for a selected x86-64 CPU target
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B scripts/kagi-build
.RI [ cargo-build-arguments ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Appends CPU targeting flags to
.B RUSTFLAGS
and invokes
.B cargo build \-\-release
from the repository root.
Additional arguments are passed to Cargo.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B KAGI_CPU_TARGET
Choose
.B portable
(the default),
.BR native ,
.BR avx2 ,
.BR avx512 ,
.BR avx10.1 ,
or
.BR avx10.2 .
Deploy a nonportable build only on CPUs supporting its selected features.
The helper checks that the Rust toolchain recognizes AVX10 before using
an AVX10 target.
.TP
.B RUSTFLAGS
Existing Rust compiler flags.
The selected CPU flags are appended to this value.
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
KAGI_CPU_TARGET=portable scripts/kagi-build \-\-locked \-\-bin kagi-config
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR kagi-bench (1),
.BR test-all (1)
